{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966420-mage-chronicle-ideas","id":966420,"title":"Mage Chronicle Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-09T13:53:24-07:00","id":966420,"title":"Mage Chronicle Ideas","content":"So, this thread is for various Chronicle and Setting ideas, for Storytellers in a rush or just looking for inspiration can drop by and use/adapt something.<br /> <br /> I'll post a few ideas in a bit, once I have them written down elsewhere (so the forum/browser doesn't eat my text again). <hr /><br /> <b>Ravenstone Academy</b><br /> <br /> The basic setting is that of an upper-to-middle class school. What makes this learning complex unique is that it is populated by the members of a number of Proximus Dynasties that are unusually concentrated in the area. Classes include the normal subjects one would expect in addition to studies on the Arcana and supernatural phenomena. Social troubles are typical high school and collegiate drama, in addition to politicking between to competitive families.<br /> <br /> Characters are Proximi (or possibly Sleepwalkers - not all Dynasty members become Proximi, after all). Plots can include personal and interpersonal teen drama, dealing with escaped experiments and Paradoxes gone wrong, and external intrusions into this insular community.<br /> <br /> [Feel free to add specific characters, plots, and Proximus Dynasties. And yes, this is Awakening!Hogwarts, or any other &quot;magic school&quot; concept. Combined with a little inter-noble fighting.] <hr /><br /> <b>Proximus Cyberware, Ltd.</b><br /> <br /> For those waiting for Deviant, this one has the PCs as &quot;Cybernetically Enhanced&quot; and &quot;Biologically Modified&quot; individuals, largely oppossing and/or on the run from massive conspiracies. The Modified are built as Proximi, with the Blessings as the Cyber/Bio-ware (Pre-defined lists justified as only those augmentations being compatible with a given &quot;design&quot;), the Curse as the inherent defect in the procedure/design, Reach as &quot;overclocking&quot; your mods, and Paradox as that blowing up in your face. Arcane Experiences exist and are available as actual research material and items stolen/traded from the conspiracies.<br /> <br /> [It's up the the individual STs if these mods are actually artifical Supernal magic masquerading as implants/mods (and thus subject to Paradox and Dissonance as normal), separate and just using the Proximus/Arcana rules (and thus not subject to Paradox beyond where relevant for Proximi, or Dissonance), or a combination (Supernal magic that evades the Lie through this new method, or alternative answers for Dissonance and Paradox, like Conspiracy Clean Up Crews).]<br /> <br /> [Considering most tech/mods are usually more rigid than spells, STs might want to opt into more strictly defined limits on the Blessings/Mods, perhaps in exchange for free Reach effects.] <hr />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-09-2016, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:27:11-07:00","id":966983,"title":"","content":"<b>Consilium Gregis Lupini</b><br /> <i>(Werewolf-Mage Chronicle)</i><br /> <br /> Some places have a dark history and the past of this small town threw the Shadow into complete chaos. Loci are everywhere and spirits stalk the streets. The Forsaken who lived here struggle to hold out against the rising spirit tide. Very few of the awakened take notice of this small town, for while it may be unnatural there is very little mystery to draw the average mage out of curiosity alone. With so few mages and werewolves they have combined together in an unusual alliance, a consilium that consists of both cabals and packs. A place where the line between the two begins to blur and cabals take on Totems and packs pick their symbolic themes.<br /> <br /> Into this strange culture the next generation brings things further than the elders ever expected as several young Mages and Werewolves fresh from their awakenings and first changes have banded together into something that isn't quite a pack or a cabal. Many have their doubts about the wisdom or harmony of such a group, but is that just a conservative nature or based on real dangers. Can this new group win the trust and support of their colleagues and prove that wolf and man have more in common than people expect? What does it mean to be one of the Wise or the children of Luna and does it actually have anything to do with how you were born?<br /> <br /> This is just a simple justification to run a werewolf-mage crossover chronicle. Not all Mages would need to be Thyrsus, but taking a dot or two in spirit would be best to keep everyone capable of interacting with the shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:02:03-07:00","id":966998,"title":"","content":"<b>Supernal Summoners</b><br /> <br /> Either as a setting-wide thing, or just a local phenomena, some Sleepwalkers have the ability to Bond with Supernal Entities, treating them as Familiars/Retainers and portecting them from the ravages of the Fallen world. PCs are Sleepwalkers with this trait that lets them engage in a Bond with a willing (or defeated?) Supernal entity (usually one from one of the nearby Verges). Once Bonded, the Supernal is free from being destroyed from being in the Fallen World, though they must largely heed the requests of their Sleepwalker (provided they have the Mana and the ability).<br /> <br /> [Supernal beings have tremendous power in their Arcana due to free Reach, but this is mitigated by Sleepwalkers not possessing an intuitive understanding of each Arcana's capabilities.]<br /> <br /> [Intended for a focus on who/what the character has bound and their nature with it as a gateway to power, rather than just the powers themselves. But, hey, if you want to turn it into Mage-Pokemon, feel free.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T06:14:44-07:00","id":967883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966420-mage-chronicle-ideas?p=966998#post966998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [Intended for a focus on who/what the character has bound and their nature with it as a gateway to power, rather than just the powers themselves. But, hey, if you want to turn it into Mage-Pokemon, feel free.]</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw it more as Mage-Shin Megami Tensei or Mage-Fate/Stay Night, personally.<br /> <br /> <b>Vox Populi</b><br /> The city of Monterey is considered the \u201cLanguage Capital of the World,\u201d and given that people from across the world come to the Language Institute to learn from one of its 1900 instructors, this epithet is well deserved. However, this has resulted (or is the result of, Mysterium research into the phenomenon isn\u2019t sure) in one of the most curious Mysteries of the modern day. On occasion, people within the city experience xenoglossia, the phenomenon wherein a person suddenly knows how to speak and understand a language that they could not possibly have learned naturally. Even stranger, whenever a person experiences this, everyone in the immediate vicinity who shares an understanding of the speaker\u2019s native language will also be affected. Throughout the period of xenoglossia, no one seems to be aware that they are not, in fact, speaking their intended language. The only people who are aware of the phenomenon are Sleepwalkers and the Awakened. Sleepers, even ones who do not share an understanding of the speaker\u2019s intended language, hear nothing out of the ordinary. Even stranger, this xenoglossia does not extend to the written word, but does extend to the thoughts of the user. In essence, for short periods, people suddenly have their native language replaced with one completely foreign to them.<br /> <br /> This xenoglossia does follow a few additional rules which make its study harder. It never gives a person access to a language that someone in the area considers a native language. The extent of this effect appears to vary based on ambient noise rather than anything else. Essentially, if a person can reasonably hear the speaker, the xenoglossia never selects his native language. It also does not seem to afflict people who are being recorded, whether they are aware of the recording or not. With the advent of cell phone cameras and the more widespread use of security cameras, the Mysterium fears that this particular Mystery may be stamped out before they can understand it. And then there\u2019s what happens when someone has Dark Angel Aphasia\u2026<br /> <br /> Doesn't have to be Monterey, though that bit is actually true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}